id: pm-m1tfmp
title: Recover telemetry metrics from a non-sequential Prometheus WAL
description: "Live operational verification found Prometheus repeatedly aborting with opening storage failed: get segment range: segments are not sequential. Ingestion API, worker, Postgres and broker are healthy, with an empty event queue. Recover monitoring through a preservation-first procedure and verify live metrics separately from durable command event pairing."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[1]: changelog-exclude
created_at: "2026-10-12T21:48:16.899Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T22:58:18.102Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T22:56:14.868Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T22:56:14.868Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Preserve and verify the complete original TSDB before reversible recovery; keep immutable blocks and Postgres telemetry intact; restore ready metrics and healthy scrape targets; record the recovered-head time-window limitation and rollback evidence privately.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Moved the verified TSDB copy to supported local POSIX storage; retained the original data and quarantined obsolete WAL/mmap cache segments, then replayed the retained checkpoint/WAL. Preventive guard is tracked in pm-xa1w84."
expected_result: Prometheus starts safely and receives fresh scrapes without discarding historical data.
actual_result: "All 1451 file hashes matched before switching storage. Retained checkpoint/WAL replay completed; ready HTTP 200, six of six targets healthy with fresh timestamps, 5017 active series, about 334 samples/second and zero restarts. Original data and quarantined caches remain preserved."
